TIP:  For the intro, pick the note and strum the chord.  For the (D) it's the open 4th string and open 5th string.  Do this twice.

TIP:  (D4) is just (D) with the pinky added (and removed) from the 1st string/3rd fret while holding position.  Same thing with the (A) and (A6) with the pinky added (and removed) below the ring finger on the 1st string/2nd fret.  For the (G4), hold the 1st string and swing your index finger over to the 2nd string/1st fret (c) note.  The finger can come off the top string.  Or you can just play a (C).  


